Subject: [PATCH] docs: drop the deleted WPF adapter from the public surface
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Batch 3b of the root repository's test-suite retirement item.

Broiler.HTML.WPF was removed, but the repository still advertised it. The
README described the renderer as ending in "WPF hosting", listed the assembly
among the shipped set, and documented four public types on it; the architecture
notes named it as one of the two concrete backends hosting pipeline output and
gave it its own hosting section; and two gate lists still required WPF checks to
pass. None of it exists.

Three assemblies also still granted it internals access. Those
InternalsVisibleTo("Broiler.HTML.WPF") entries in Broiler.HTML.Core,
Broiler.HTML.Dom, and Broiler.HTML.Orchestration named an assembly that is never
built, so they widened nothing — but a friend grant to a non-existent assembly
is an invitation to recreate it, and the root repository's Skia decoupling guard
asserted on the deleted directory's continued existence until this cleanup.

Two "without WPF" qualifiers on Broiler.HTML.Graphics are also dropped: with no
WPF frontend left, rendering without it is not a distinguishing property.

The Win32 demo and the Direct2D surface are untouched; only the WPF half of
those sentences goes.

